# Read by Cloudflare's static assets (wrangler.toml [assets]); other hosts ignore it.
# Vercel gets the same rule from vercel.json.
#
# Everything under /assets/ is a built file whose NAME contains a hash of its
# contents: a changed file has a different name, so a cached one is never stale.
# Without this the host sends `max-age=0, must-revalidate` and the browser asks the
# server about every one of them, on every page load, before using its copy.
#
# One DAY, not a year with `immutable`, and that is deliberate. This app rewrites
# unknown URLs to index.html, so a tab left open across a deploy that asks for a
# file the deploy deleted gets a 200 with HTML instead of a 404 -- and with a
# year-long lifetime the browser would keep that wrong answer for a year, which
# bites if a later deploy (a rollback, say) brings that exact file name back. A day
# bounds it. The saving, which is skipping the per-file check for visits within a
# day, is the same either way for anyone who comes back that often.
#
# NOT applied to index.html (it names the current files, so it must always be
# checked) or to /sfx/ (those file names carry no hash).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Security headers, on every response. Vercel gets the same set from vercel.json
# (tests/security-headers.test.mjs keeps the two identical).
#
# Permissions-Policy: camera, microphone and screen capture are allowed for this
# site ONLY, because voice, video calls, blur and screen share need them. Taking
# "(self)" off any of these silently breaks calling. Location, payment and USB are
# never used, so they are off.
#
# Referrer-Policy: invite links carry a secret in the path (/invite/<token>). Other
# sites must only ever be told the origin, never the path.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: Content-Security-Policy (needs a signed-in test of sign-in,
# Firestore, GIFs, voice and blur before it can be enforced) and a
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy (the Google sign-in popup would break).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), display-capture=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
